        {
          "username": "Sunayan Bhattacharjee",
          "rating": 5,
          "contributor_id": "107294471312635716921",
          "user_review_count": 346,
          "user_photo_count": 3903,
          "user_thumbnail": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXCp8nAn3xkptMjFuwYttJbwpPhk8nY7DqGbtRcspvreOol4dI=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100",
          "description": "As diehard foodies, my partner and I are quite aware of the good restaurants in and around Bengaluru. We had been hearing a lot about the different outlets of ‘Kapoor’s Café.’ In fact, we spotted the Yelahanka outlet just opposite to ‘The Galleria Mall’ on quite a few occasions. That and the fact that many acquaintances have spoken well of the eatery inspired us to visit the Yelahanka outlet yesterday (Saturday – March 14, 2026). One look at the restaurant and we were quite impressed with the décor. The way different kinds of posters were hung showed that quite a bit of thoughts was put into the making of the café. Anyway, both of us went for the Thali options. While my partner ordered the ‘Matar Paneer Combo,’ I went ahead with the more experimental ‘Palak Paneer Combo.’ Alongside, we also ordered two (2) glasses of ‘Lassi Gur Wali’ and a bottle of the eatery’s own brand of drinking water. All the items on the two thalis were excellent. What impressed us the most was the ‘Lassi Gur Wali.’ It was nothing short of being magical. The taste was absolutely authentic. I could have had it anywhere in Punjab as well. Subject to the shortage of LPG Gas Cylinders, the thalis took a bit of time to arrive. Else, everything was simply spot on. The bill amount was also not that high. Overall, it was a very satisfactory experience for both of us. In the future, we would like to visit the other outlets of the eatery. Cheers!",
